  "answer": "I'll start by reading the bug-diagnosis skill and locating how special prices are applied on the storefront.The discount is dropped in two places: the admin mapper stores the end date on the start-date field, and price calculation then compares the start date to itself. I'll fix both and add a regression test.Special prices that included an end date never reached the storefront as a discount. Creating a product stored the end date in the start-date field, and the catalogue price calculation then required the start date to be both before and after today, so the special amount was ignored. The end date is now saved on the end-date field, and a current special is applied when that end date is still in the future. Undated specials are unchanged.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceDiscountTest,PersistableProductAvailabilityMapperTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"live admin and storefront HTTP APIs\"], \"missing\": [\"an integration fixture that creates a product through the admin REST API and reads it back from the storefront API\"]}",
